.TH OPENWITTY-TRAY 1 "November 2026" "openwitty 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openwitty-tray \- OpenWitty status icon for the system tray (unofficial, experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openwitty-tray
.RB [ \-\-wait\-for\-tray\-seconds " n] [" \-\-quit "] [" \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
An optional status icon for the desktop's system tray (KDE Plasma and other desktops that provide a
Status Notifier host). Its tooltip and menu show whether the speaker volume knob is shown in the desktop
volume and whether the
.BR openwitty-volumed (1)
background service runs. The menu opens OpenWitty, opens its Desktop integration settings, or quits the
icon. A left click opens OpenWitty. An OpenWitty window that is already open is brought to the front
instead of starting a second one.
.PP
The tray icon never opens the CONNECT 2, never reads the desktop mixer and never starts, stops or changes
the background service: it reads only the OpenWitty settings file and \fBsystemctl \-\-user show\fR.
Quitting it removes only the icon; closing the OpenWitty window does not stop the service either.
.PP
It is not started automatically after installation. Turn on \fIShow OpenWitty in the system tray\fR in
OpenWitty under Settings \(-> Desktop integration to start it now and at every login; turning it off removes
the login entry and quits a running icon. Only one tray icon runs per session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-wait\-for\-tray\-seconds " n"
At login the system tray may appear a little later: wait up to n seconds (0\-300, default 30). Without a
system tray the program then exits quietly; OpenWitty itself works without it.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Ask a running tray icon to quit, then exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/io.github.st0nebyte.openwitty-tray.desktop
The login entry, present only while the setting is on.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/openwitty/openwitty.conf
OpenWitty settings (read only).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openwitty (1),
.BR openwitty-volumed (1)
